# Call a Surprise Witness: "Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.
# Put a flying counter on it. It's a Spirit in addition to its other types."
# Bot1 casts Hired Blade (mana value 3) and Questing Beast (mana value 4) on turn 1; Bot2 casts an Ornithopter on turn 2;
# Bot1's Wrath of God on turn 3 puts all three creature cards in graveyards, with Black Lotus (a noncreature card of mana
# value 0, sacrificed for mana) already in Bot1's. On turn 5 the Witness is refused for each of those but the right one:
# Questing Beast (4 is over the limit), Bot2's Ornithopter (not Bot1's graveyard, though 0 is under it), Black Lotus (not
# a creature). Hired Blade, at exactly 3, comes back: a 3/2 with a flying counter (so it has flying, CR 122.1b) and the
# Spirit type added to Human Assassin (CR 205.1b, 611.2a), beside the Flash it already had.

